Dear Julia,

sorry, but no. We are just not fans of online/hybrid courses. Admittedly, an online option would carry benefits for people who cannot physically attend. However, for us and for the people who do physically attend, it would entail substantial costs: having to cater for an online audience completely changes the whole character of a course as a lively event with direct interactions between humans. We do like this human side of a course very much, as it allows for far richer forms of communication and exchange.

Best regards  --- Marc

